		{
			title: "Too Easy? Too Difficult?"
			icon: {
				id: "ae2:fluix_sword"
				Count: 1b
				tag: {
					Damage: 0
				}
			}
			x: 1.25d
			y: -2.25d
			shape: "rsquare"
			subtitle: "A Personal Challenge"
			description: [
				"&5That's different. Hey sis, it looks like they let you choose how difficult things are inside the Vaults."
				""
				"&dProbably as a way to keep as many players as possible. Vault Hunters looks like it can be very difficult, so giving players the ability to make their game easier and more enjoyable keeps them interested longer."
				""
				"&5Do Power Users like Bandit even get a choice?"
				""
				"&dYeah, looks like they can. Might as well take advantage of it, Bandit, if things are too hard or too easy."
				""
				"You can set your world or server's game mode by using the following : "
				""
				"&6/gamerule VaultMode Normal :&r The default mode. If you die in a Vault, you get a Spirit with your equipment, and have to pay Vault Gold to get your stuff back."
				""
				"&6/gamerule VaultMode Casual :&r You get your items back if you die, but they take some durability damage."
				""
				"&6/gamerule VaultMode Hardcore :&r You lose everything on you if you die in a Vault. "
			]
			hide_dependency_lines: true
			dependencies: ["6DEFECFABD4DCB59"]
			hide: true
			id: "4CA0844372B19F19"
			tasks: [{
				id: "61503165E064852F"
				type: "checkmark"
				title: "Advent of Information"
			}]
